From c18727cce7ceff53ab8da83089e9f7a60e7346b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:30:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 143/144] video: a video file in a slot opens only as MP4,
 QuickTime, Matroska or WebM

A host's video file in a texture slot (a Wallpaper Engine preset's own `files/<name>.mp4`, from someone else's Workshop
item) went to avformat_open_input with every demuxer and protocol FFmpeg has: FFmpeg picks a demuxer by the bytes, not
the name, so a file named .mp4 could open as any format FFmpeg reads, a playlist among them, which opens further files
and URLs of its own.

The probe in RenderContext (videoFileTexture) and the player's decoder now open such a file only with the demuxers its
extensions name (GLPlayer::kFileFormats: mov/mp4 and matroska/webm, FFmpeg's `format_whitelist`) and the `file`
protocol alone (`protocol_whitelist`). Anything else throws AssetLoadException "Not an MP4, QuickTime, Matroska or WebM
video file", so the slot keeps its texture and the health report says why. A video texture inside a scene (its bytes
from the scene's own containers) and a video wallpaper open as before.

Tested by liascape's host_api_test usertexture_plays_a_video_file: a playable MPEG-4 stream muxed as MPEG-TS and named
.mp4 keeps the slot's white with that health line, and the same stream muxed as MP4 plays its grey; red on d4d351b
(the MPEG-TS stream took the slot: 214 214 214).

Origin: ours
Why: liascape docs/TODO.md #112 (a preset's video in a scene's texture slot plays)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5, effort high <noreply@anthropic.com>
